id: pm-web-gixc
title: Refresh connected project viewers after the realtime database listener reconnects
description: "The PostgreSQL LISTEN connection retries after a disconnect but notifications during that interval are transient and lost while browser SSE streams stay open. Workspace and Packages views can remain stale until an unrelated event or reload. After successful re-LISTEN, deliver bounded local workspace-changed and extensions-changed invalidations to every active project without publishing them to the shared bus. Reproduce lost item and package notifications using a dedicated throwaway PostgreSQL listener and real HTTP event streams."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-07T22:58:28.455Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T23:45:37.485Z"
assignee: codex-hosted-collaboration
claim_principal: codex-hosted-collaboration
author: codex-hosted-collaboration
acceptance_criteria: A real PostgreSQL disconnect followed by item and package notifications during the gap yields one workspace and one extension-catalog refresh on every still-connected project stream after LISTEN succeeds; later project notifications retain tenant isolation; initial startup and stopped listeners do not emit reconnect refreshes; installed CLI 2026.9.7 real SDK tests and release checks remain green; report remaining whole-source coverage and hosted rollout gates accurately.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-web-2rek,related,"2026-09-07T22:58:28.455Z",codex-hosted-collaboration,"cli:create:dep",detected
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T23:01:22.108Z",codex-hosted-collaboration,"TDD: dedicated PostgreSQL listener termination reproduced the missing recovery invalidation before the fix (3-second bounded assertion failed). After adding local invalidations on successful re-LISTEN, the real HTTP/PG regression passes and confirms the gap notification was lost, both active projects refresh once, recovery never echoes to the shared channel, subsequent events remain project-isolated, and stop removes delivery. Replaced the previous source-text reconnect assertion with this behavioral regression. Installed CLI/SDK is 2026.9.7. Coordinated hosted deployment and complete source coverage remain separate unfulfilled gates."
  "2026-09-07T23:07:47.782Z",codex-hosted-collaboration,"Validation 2026-09-07 UTC: npm run release:check passed (393 tests; 393 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped; all 30 configured src files reported). Measured lines/branches/functions: 71.04% / 81.17% / 65.71%; the Node reporter does not expose an independent statement metric. Realtime bus measured 93.59% / 76.79% / 78.95%. Docstring gate documents 565 declarations. Packed npm/Bun acceptance, production vulnerability audit, changelog verification, release-date and publish-attestation checks passed. PM-linked real database regression also passed. Whole-source 100% and reviewed hosted rollout remain unfulfilled and this item stays in progress until those deployment acceptance obligations are verified."
  "2026-09-07T23:23:43.923Z",codex-hosted-collaboration,"Review follow-up: CodeRabbit reported 66.67% documentation among three touched functions; the missing declaration was the existing fakeResponse unit-test sink. Added its docstring. Greptile reviewed commit 64e3208 with 5/5 confidence and no findings. Startup policy was independently checked: src/server.ts awaits startRealtimeBus before app.listen and exits on an initial listener failure, so viewers cannot be connected before first successful LISTEN. The real regression also verifies initial LISTEN does not emit a recovery event. Additional isolated transport measurement at 64e3208 connected 1000 project viewers plus 10 control viewers in 2.777 seconds, delivered 1000/1000 notifications with zero tenant crossover and p99 88.205 ms, and refreshed 1010/1010 viewers after listener recovery in 871.726 ms. This 5.404-second run measured HTTP/PostgreSQL transport only: it does not certify authentication, browser UI, live user data, write throughput, reconnection storms, or larger production capacity."
  "2026-09-07T23:41:33.818Z",codex-hosted-collaboration,"Packages recovery follow-up: source inspection confirmed that Packages listens to extensions-changed, so workspace-changed alone cannot refresh its catalog after a missed package notification. Extended the real HTTP/PostgreSQL regression first: it failed with missing Packages recovery. Added one local extensions-changed invalidation per active project alongside workspace-changed. The regression now passes and proves both notifications sent during the disconnect were lost, both recovery types arrive exactly once on each open stream, initial connection does not refresh, and no recovery notification is echoed to PostgreSQL. The full release gate and updated isolated capacity measurement follow."
  "2026-09-07T23:45:37.485Z",codex-hosted-collaboration,"Packages recovery validation: npm run release:check passed 393/393 tests, no failures or skips, all 30 configured server src files measured at 71.05% lines / 81.17% branches / 65.71% functions. Realtime bus is 93.64% / 76.79% / 78.95%. The Node reporter exposes no independent statement metric, and the configured sources exclude the public frontend. Documentation covers 86 files and 565 declarations; packed npm/Bun acceptance, production audit, changelog and release checks passed. The expanded PM-linked real HTTP/PostgreSQL acceptance passed. The updated isolated transport probe connected 1000 project viewers plus 10 control viewers, delivered to 1000/1000 with zero crossover and p99 59.982 ms, and delivered exactly 1010 workspace plus 1010 Packages recovery frames in 956.753 ms. This run measures synthetic HTTP/PostgreSQL transport only, not authenticated browser behavior or production write capacity. Whole-source 100/100/100/100, all reviewer availability, and the hosted rollout remain unmet."
